<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Konrad Adenauer</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1876–1967</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Konrad Adenauer was the first Chancellor of the Federal Republic of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, from 1949 to 1963. A former mayor of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a> removed by the Nazis, he led the Christian Democratic Union and anchored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-germany">West Germany</a> in the West through <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nato">NATO</a> membership, reconciliation with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and European integration. His governments oversaw the economic recovery known as the economic miracle.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/konrad-adenauer.jpg" alt="Konrad Adenauer" width="320" height="479" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Katherine Young (1906–1993) · CC BY-SA 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bundesarchiv_B_145_Bild-F078072-0004,_Konrad_Adenauer.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
